Alembic migrations for TePlanner backend.

Run from `backend/` (the dir alembic.ini lives in):

  alembic upgrade head             # apply all pending migrations
  alembic current                  # show current revision
  alembic history                  # show revision graph
  alembic revision -m "msg"        # new empty revision
  alembic revision --autogenerate -m "msg"   # diff Base.metadata vs DB

Bootstrap on an existing DB (one-time):
  alembic stamp head               # mark current schema as up-to-date

Baseline (0001_baseline) reflects the schema produced by
`Base.metadata.create_all` at the moment Alembic was introduced. Every
subsequent schema change must ship as a new versioned migration.
